The Pupil of the General

♫2360978174

The shadow of El Pardo was heavy and long,  
When a young prince was summoned  
to play a part wrong.  
The Generalissimo watched  
him through the years,  
To mold a successor of silence and fears.  
He took the young Bourbon and taught him to wait,  
Beside the grim gears of the fascist old state.

“Stay loyal, Juan Carlos,” the dictator said,  
“And keep the crown safe when I’m buried and dead.”  
The prince swore an oath to the system of iron,  
While the democrats cursed him as Franco’s young lion.  
But behind the calm eyes of the student in uniform,  
The king was preparing to ride out the storm.

When the old general died in the chill of the fall,  
The young monarch stepped up to answer the call.  
He dismantled the prisons, he opened the gate,  
And brought back democracy into the state.  
The right wing felt cheated, the generals grew red—  
They had fostered a wolf in the dictator’s bed.

